From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FPSensor <gkartyt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:42:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/xz_wrap.sh: Skip the BCJ filter when xz lacks it

The xz from Android's prebuilts is built without the BCJ filters and
rejects --arm with "Unsupported filter chain". The filter only helps
compression and the in-kernel decompressor handles plain LZMA2, so drop
it when the host xz can't use it.
---
 scripts/xz_wrap.sh | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/xz_wrap.sh b/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
index 7a2d372f..3910c816 100755
--- a/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
+++ b/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
@@ -20,4 +20,11 @@ case $SRCARCH in
 	sparc)          BCJ=--sparc ;;
 esac
 
+# Some xz builds (e.g. the Android prebuilt) lack the BCJ filters. The
+# filter is optional for the in-kernel decompressor, so only use it when
+# this xz supports it.
+if [ -n "$BCJ" ] && ! echo | xz --check=crc32 $BCJ --lzma2=dict=1MiB >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+	BCJ=
+fi
+
 exec xz --check=crc32 $BCJ --lzma2=$LZMA2OPTS,dict=32MiB
